'''Earnest Adams''' (born March 12, 1959) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] [[linebacker]] who primarily played in the [[United States Football League]] (USFL) for the [[Pittsburgh Maulers (1984)|Pittsburgh Maulers]] and [[Portland Breakers]], but was also a [[replacement player]] during the [[1987 NFL strike]] for the [[Detroit Lions]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL), and played for the [[Tampa Bay Storm|Pittsburgh Gladiators]] of the [[Arena Football League]] (AFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Illinois Fighting Illini football|Illinois Fighting Illini]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Earnest Adams Stats, Height, Weight, Position, Draft, College |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/A/AdamEa20.htm |access-date=September 23, 2022 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Earnest Adams NFL Stats - Pro Football Archives |url=https://www.profootballarchives.com/playera/adam02350.html |access-date=September 23, 2022 |website=www.profootballarchives.com |archive-date=September 23, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220923224902/https://www.profootballarchives.com/playera/adam02350.html |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Earnest Adams football Statistics on StatsCrew.com |url=https://www.statscrew.com/football/stats/p-adamsear001 |access-date=September 23, 2022 |website=www.statscrew.com |language=en}}</ref>
